# 24.11 What’s wrong with this picture?
* probability that Y defective items will be found in a sample of size n, given that the proportion of defective items in the
lot is π = 0.05 = 0.05
pie = 0.05 = 0.05
Pr0_31 = MATH.PMF.BIN(pie,31,0) = 0.20390682574579
Pr0_34 = MATH.PMF.BIN(pie,34,0) = 0.174824614723797
Pr0_59 = MATH.PMF.BIN(pie,59,0) = 0.0484945252494231
Pr0_65 = MATH.PMF.BIN(pie,65,0) = 0.0356479322505602
Pr1_31 = MATH.PMF.BIN(pie,31,1) = 0.332690084111554
Pr1_34 = MATH.PMF.BIN(pie,34,1) = 0.31284404740048
Pr1_59 = MATH.PMF.BIN(pie,59,1) = 0.150588262616626
Pr2_59 = MATH.PMF.BIN(pie,59,2) = 0.22984524294117
* probability of occurrence of each of the four events
Pr_Ev1 = Pr0_59 = 0.0484945252494231
Pr_Ev2 = Pr1_59*Pr0_34 = 0.0263265349938776
Pr_Ev3 = Pr2_59*Pr0_65 = 0.00819350764848038
Pr_Ev4 = Pr1_59*Pr1_34*Pr0_31 = 0.00960618138097685
Pr_LotAccept = Pr_Ev1 + Pr_Ev2 + Pr_Ev3 + Pr_Ev4 = 0.0926207492727579
Assurance = 1 - Pr_LotAccept = 0.907379250727242
